#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:5
#: 2cea9f09992c4992aa632a7f650d3f8d
msgid "Electronic Speed Controller (ESC) Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:7
#: 2484d3f9371b4282bdd8a10b965d008b
msgid "This document applies ONLY to Copter setups, not Rover or Plane. Refer to those vehicles setup guides for ESC calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:9
#: 0a01b1fd12594fe9b87d1f8e7933885d
msgid "Electronic speed controllers are responsible for spinning the motors at the speed requested by the autopilot. Most ESCs need to be calibrated so that they know the minimum and maximum pwm values that the flight controller will send.  This page provides instructions for calibrating ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:17
#: b3154f727db844e082f93f2edbfea4ec
msgid "Please complete :ref:`radio calibration <common-radio-control-calibration>` before performing ESC calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:21
#: 7db2ab1126f748d0aa5f438d7cff311f
msgid "About ESC Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:23
#: 0c38fccaa4be4ed8abf9ec0e84081e0c
msgid "ESC calibration will vary based on what brand of ESC you are using, so always refer to the documentation for the brand of ESC you are using for specific information (such as tones).  \"All at once\" calibration works well for most ESCs, so it is good idea to attempt it first and if that fails try the \"Manual ESC-by-ESC\" method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:29
#: f5dc717b8e8f44d29815842a9341eba6
msgid "Refer to :ref:`common-brushless-escs` for setup of the ESC protocol (:ref:`MOT_PWM_TYPE <MOT_PWM_TYPE>`) according to your type of ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:30
#: 218495efbbb7496aa117845fb2fb94a4
msgid "Some ESCs like the DJI Opto ESCs do not require and do not support calibration, so skip this page completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:31
#: 13f6bc76ed304f689e643dd3208d59e6
msgid "If you are using a digital esc protocol like DShot or are using CAN ESCs then you also don't need to calibrate them, so skip this page. The section at the end on ESC settings is still applicable, however."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:32
#: afdbf8abfac6441099fe0155744a3503
msgid "Some brands of ESC do not allow calibration and will not arm unless you adjust your radio's throttle end-points so that the minimum throttle is around 1000 PWM and maximum is around 2000.  Note that if you change the end-points on your TX you must re-do the :ref:`Radio Calibration <common-radio-control-calibration>`.  Alternatively, you may manually set the :ref:`MOT_PWM_MIN <MOT_PWM_MIN>` to 1000 and :ref:`MOT_PWM_MAX <MOT_PWM_MAX>` to 2000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:33
#: 143535854bed4f7fbff8c0ecbedb65cb
msgid "Begin this procedure only after you have completed the :ref:`radio control calibration <common-radio-control-calibration>` and :ref:`Connect ESCs and motors <connect-escs-and-motors>` part of the :ref:`Autopilot System Assembly Instructions <autopilot-assembly-instructions>`.  Next follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:37
#: 9cf7b3fa9a19448f82c913e39044c8c1
msgid "**Safety Check!**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:39
#: 80bc7f51d16d4d688e46be58c39d0184
msgid "Before calibrating ESCs, please ensure that your copter has NO PROPS on it and that the autopilot is NOT CONNECTED to your computer via USB and the Lipo battery is disconnected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:52
#: 280e8c5e4e2d4ad191c378f2ad99327e
msgid "All at once calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:54
#: 514e9996cc6341aea24a27bb40a57c36
msgid "Turn on your transmitter and put the throttle stick at maximum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:60
#: 5abc625441a04659b09ffc8cf3c1b498
msgid "Connect the Lipo battery.  The autopilot's red, blue and yellow LEDs will light up in a cyclical pattern. This means the it's ready to go into ESC calibration mode the next time you plug it in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:68
#: 2c7ee308ed1f43e589b8de410a0ee825
msgid "With the transmitter throttle stick still high, disconnect and reconnect the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:79
#: 14ff936cd2864f2bbb57beee42643dd4
msgid "For Autopilots with a safety switch, push it until the LED displays solid red"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:80
#: 4134208623424885baa6c65f5e8b60cf
msgid "The autopilot is now in ESC calibration mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:81
#: 01efb5315b6b44eb9f448382cb65a271
msgid "Wait for your ESCs to emit the musical tone, the regular number of beeps indicating your battery's cell count (i.e. 3 for 3S, 4 for 4S) and then an additional two beeps to indicate that the maximum throttle has been captured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:85
#: dfb95459395d45d49d5efb5b429e5f5a
msgid "Pull the transmitter's throttle stick down to its minimum position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:91
#: 96a084dc48ed429e8a242122590abc67
msgid "The ESCs should then emit a long tone indicating that the minimum throttle has been captured and the calibration is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:93
#: 0d496105d81d4ba5ab9bf32d173ed816
msgid "If the long tone indicating successful calibration was heard, the ESCs are \"live\" now and if you raise the throttle a bit they should spin. Test that the motors spin by raising the throttle a bit and then lowering it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:97
#: c5a03a0dd687416f88c05d661606d5b1
msgid "Set the throttle to minimum and disconnect the battery to exit ESC-calibration mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:100
#: a3d69525467041b0903705a8129c7697
msgid "**Here is a video demonstrating the process:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:106
#: e079ab3c83464b1fa16db94b69ebf1a1
msgid "Manual ESC-by-ESC Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:108
#: 34486553777542f08ed53a8aa10f8ad7
msgid "Plug one of your ESC three-wire cables into the throttle channel of the RC receiver. (This is usually channel 3.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:110
#: 1f61e9fbdfbb4ab2981babb8a985bed5
msgid "Turn on the transmitter and set throttle stick to maximum (full up)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:111
#: 522cee2e85e54fb99f2bbfe7541d569d
msgid "Connect the LiPo battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:112
#: fab44b00c80348f6a38a5bd58ce648e1
msgid "You will hear a musical tone then two beeps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:113
#: c184ccf73d2a449293ba8974e3e893b4
msgid "After the two beeps, lower the throttle stick to full down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:114
#: a5f3ef43f5174808b0acd145c0afe323
msgid "You will then hear a number of beeps (one for each battery cell you're using) and finally a single long beep indicating the end points have been set and the ESC is calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:117
#: 05073764d8ef4d15a6301f0a32ee6f97
msgid "Disconnect battery. Repeat these steps for all ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:118
#: 8bf3c948e25a4af28516484a3b00f6c3
msgid "If it appears that the ESC’s did not calibrate then the throttle channel on the transmitter might need to be reversed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:120
#: 07862bec1772463a8d82ced2e23229f8
msgid "If you are still having trouble after trying these methods (for example, ESCs still beep continuously) try lowering your throttle trim 50%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:123
#: 1d934dba96134628a767437dcc52dbea
msgid "You can also try powering your ArduPilot board via the USB first to boot it up before plugging in the LiPo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:127
#: c8600897383e49c88e41495c0622bca1
msgid "Semi Automatic ESC-by-ESC Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:129
#: b364a44277fa4fd1a48b8a0dba97b0a5
msgid "Connect to the autopilot from a ground station such as the Mission Planner and set the :ref:`ESC_CALIBRATION <ESC_CALIBRATION>` parameter to 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:130
#: 39bbe817111f4a118c44d3dcdb861fc0
msgid "Disconnect the battery and USB cable so the autopilot powers down"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:131
#: 97f557b959864739b3419f06e050ce07
msgid "Connect the battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:132
#: eaedb419fd81474c806361812d2da558
msgid "The arming tone will be played (if the vehicle has a buzzer attached)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:133
#: 3f9e2f002463497d8ead3b09242fab96
msgid "If using an autopilot with a safety button (like the Pixhawk) press it until it displays solid red"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:134
#: 90ca6ec545d14e369dae434125d11bab
msgid "You will hear a musical tone then two beeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:135
#: 67abc99f04224498b6121958167fb2bf
msgid "A few seconds later you should hear a number of beeps (one for each battery cell you're using) and finally a single long beep indicating the end points have been set and the ESC is calibrated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:136
#: 8b523c20f01c4d85bbc90b39323a7614
msgid "Disconnect the battery and power up again normally and test as described below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:139
#: e5ade9bebd204af49238a4dadbd6338b
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:141
#: b89eb0836bfe4447af4c71ae42cdfcdd
msgid "Once you have calibrated your ESCs, you can test them by plugging in your LiPo.  Remember: no propellers!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:144
#: 2c9cd40227794ff5b4f016f702ee88f5
msgid "Ensure your transmitter's flight mode switch is set to “Stabilize Mode”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:146
#: 2f8a16bda49449099889d350c63e2fd3
msgid ":ref:`Arm your copter <arming_the_motors>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:147
#: b6eb4f921980466bb4ccd687ba91ccb1
msgid "Give a small amount of throttle.  All motors should spin at about same speed and they should start at the same time. If the motors do not all start at the same time and spin at the same speed, the ESC’s are still not properly calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:151
#: 135b89dceab4492ab848d2a30453c5ae
msgid "Disarm your copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:154
#: 8a609637012d497cac12f246f7bc3122
msgid "Notes / Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:156
#: 81f98267c4324af4bf02272fbdc15440
msgid "The All-at-once ESC calibration mode simply causes the autopilot to pass through the pilot's throttle directly through to the ESCs. If you power up the autopilot while in this mode you’ll send the same PWM signal to all the ESCs. That's all it does.  Many ESCs use full throttle at startup to enter programming mode, full throttle position is then saved as the upper end point and when you pull the throttle down to zero, that position is saved as the lower end point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:164
#: b324e93b20974e67b21eb7ec208fc863
msgid "If after calibration your motors do NOT spin same speed nor start at the same time, repeat the calibration process. If you tried the auto calibration above and it didn’t work or the ESCs do not drive the motors identically, try the manual calibration method described above. That should work almost every time. (Rarely after a full manual calibration you will also need to do an additional final automatic calibration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:171
#: 69b8915984aa42f59e326432ddbc9a1c
msgid "Finally, there are a huge number of brands and types of ESCs available and some of them do not adhere to the normal programming conventions (sometimes even though they claim to) and they may simply not work with ArduPilot the way it is now. This is an unfortunately necessary but true disclaimer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:178
#: 04b8babc34d04c56b38a2d96f3ddc462
msgid "Recommended ESC settings as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:180
#: 67dd2955744c44d7a10a9d73a09206db
msgid "Brake on stop: OFF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:181
#: 706362bafb1d485996a6544396d5b105
msgid "Active braking/\"Damped light\": ON (Also known as \"Non Damped mode\" set to OFF)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:182
#: 99f89a12dbec49a1816b9281069049ef
msgid "Low voltage protection: OFF (alternatively, you can set battery type to Ni-xx(NiMH or NiCd) (even if you're using Li-po batteries because this setting reduces the likelihood that the ESC's low voltage detection will turn off the motors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:186
#: ea6cc1878e9a493cbb7c924b96f082bf
msgid "CutOff Mode: Soft-Cut (Default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:187
#: a10c19e5e1044ddabbd8b1373a552b49
msgid "CutOff Threshold: Low"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:188
#: 225b204c754e441fa747b98214f61ceb
msgid "Start Mode: Normal (Default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/esc-calibration.rst:189
#: eb0f5723d13b40d48a3c46ed3c2fed6f
msgid "Timing: MEDIUM"
msgstr ""
